{%- comment -%}
  Kept deliberately, and not yet called from anywhere.

  Local pickup, for the product page block that will host it.

  Theme Check reports this as `OrphanedSnippet`, and that report is correct:
  nothing calls it yet. It is a warning, not an error, and it stands until the
  file is wired up - which is the fix, rather than silencing the check.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% doc %}
  Renders the local pickup panel for a variant.

  Shopify owns this data. `<pickup-availability>` requests
  `/variants/{id}/?section_id=pickup-availability` and Shopify returns the
  current availability for every location, already translated and already
  respecting the merchant's pickup settings.

  The theme computes nothing here — it cannot know a store's opening hours or its
  stock by location, and a theme that guessed would send customers to a shop that
  does not have the item.

  Hidden until the first response arrives, so no empty panel appears on a store
  that has pickup switched off.

  @param {variant} variant

  @example
    {% render 'pickup-availability', variant: product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- if variant != blank -%}
  <pickup-availability
    class="pickup-availability"
    data-base-url="{{ shop.url }}{{ routes.root_url }}"
    data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}"
    data-available="{{ variant.available }}"
    hidden
  >
    <div data-ref="content" data-pickup-content></div>
  </pickup-availability>
{%- endif -%}
